OL,3,V}yyy5CThursday
OL,5,G1830 Omid Djalili: Namaste
OL,6,     F1/4. Omid explores identity,
OL,7,     Fstereotypes and first impressions,
OL,8,     Ffrom growing up as the son of
OL,9,     FIranian immigrants to the
OL,10,     Fassumptions we all make about one
OL,11,     Fanother.
OL,12,G1900 The Archers
OL,13,     FAlan attempts to offer some
OL,14,     Fcomfort, and Khalil has
OL,15,     Freservations.
OL,16,G1915 Front Row
OL,17,     FTom Sutcliffe and guests review
OL,18,     Fthe Bayeux Tapestry at the British
OL,19,     FMuseum, the new novel from Rebecca
OL,20,     FF Kuang, and we reveal the
OL,21,     Fshortlist for the BBC's National
OL,22,     FShort Story Award.
OL,23,VpppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppG19/19
